From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:10:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] uml: virtio_uml: unregister a command-line device only once

At power off the exit call removes every command-line device: the
platform driver is unregistered, which deletes the virtqueues of each
device, and the devices are unregistered after it. Deleting the
virtqueues disables the rings and sends a GET_FEATURES round trip, and a
backend that goes while that is on the wire is a lost connection.
vhost_user_check_reset() then queues conn_broken_wk, which breaks the
virtio device and unregisters the same platform device a second time,
while the exit call unregisters it too. The second unregistration
finds the sysfs entries gone and dereferences NULL in
kernfs_find_and_get_ns(), "Segfault with no mm" from the events
worker, and it frees the socket path twice.

Stop the work before the exit call removes anything:
disable_work_sync() waits for one that is running, drops one that is
queued and makes every later schedule_work() a no-op, so a device is
unregistered by the work or by the exit call, never by both.

A device that is being removed has nothing left to break or unregister,
so virtio_uml_remove() clears registered first, and a connection lost
while its virtqueues are deleted queues nothing. The work itself
tolerates a device whose driver is already unbound.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c b/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c
index d2eaa488d5f0d1cffab4619e448f3ed7a1f074c9..5dd36977162158fca1a02a7fd32be40552af3ba3 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c
@@ -1738,6 +1738,12 @@ static void virtio_uml_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct virtio_uml_device *vu_dev = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	/*
+	 * A device that is being removed has nothing left to break or to
+	 * unregister: a connection lost while its virtqueues are deleted must
+	 * not queue the work that unregisters the device a second time.
+	 */
+	vu_dev->registered = 0;
 	unregister_virtio_device(&vu_dev->vdev);
 }
 
@@ -1774,7 +1780,9 @@ static void vu_conn_broken(struct work_struct *wk)
 
 	vu_dev = platform_get_drvdata(pdata->pdev);
 
-	virtio_break_device(&vu_dev->vdev);
+	/* The driver may already be unbound from a device that was removed. */
+	if (vu_dev)
+		virtio_break_device(&vu_dev->vdev);
 
 	vu_unregister_cmdline_device(&pdata->pdev->dev, NULL);
 }
@@ -1871,6 +1879,27 @@ __uml_help(vu_cmdline_param_ops,
 );
 
 
+static int vu_disable_cmdline_conn_broken(struct device *dev, void *data)
+{
+	struct platform_device *pdev = to_platform_device(dev);
+	struct virtio_uml_platform_data *pdata = pdev->dev.platform_data;
+
+	disable_work_sync(&pdata->conn_broken_wk);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Wait for the work of a lost connection that is running, drop the one that
+ * is queued, and refuse the ones to come, so that a device is unregistered by
+ * one path only: the work or the caller's.
+ */
+static void vu_disable_cmdline_conn_broken_work(void)
+{
+	if (vu_cmdline_parent_registered)
+		device_for_each_child(&vu_cmdline_parent, NULL,
+				      vu_disable_cmdline_conn_broken);
+}
+
 static void vu_unregister_cmdline_devices(void)
 {
 	if (vu_cmdline_parent_registered) {
@@ -1953,6 +1982,12 @@ static int __init virtio_uml_init(void)
 
 static void __exit virtio_uml_exit(void)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Removing a device sends its backend messages, and a backend that
+	 * goes while they are sent queues the work that unregisters the
+	 * device. That work must be over before the devices are removed here.
+	 */
+	vu_disable_cmdline_conn_broken_work();
 	platform_driver_unregister(&virtio_uml_driver);
 	vu_unregister_cmdline_devices();
 }
